# Pinned chain for ncert.nic.in (used by factory/ingest.py via verify=).
# Why: NCERT serves its Let's Encrypt leaf (CN=ncert.nic.in, issuer CN=YE1) WITHOUT
# the intermediate, so stock verifiers fail with 'unable to get local issuer certificate'.
# Chain: leaf -> YE1 -> Root YE -> ISRG Root X2 (cross-signature; Root X1 kept for safety).
# Built 2026-11-02 from the certs' own AIA URIs (http://ye1.i.lencr.org/, http://ye.i.lencr.org/).
# If NCERT reissues its cert, regenerate:
#   openssl s_client -connect ncert.nic.in:443 -servername ncert.nic.in </dev/null 2>/dev/null | openssl x509 -noout -issuer -ext authorityInfoAccess
#   curl -sS <AIA-URI> | openssl x509 -inform DER   # then append the new issuer PEM here
